# Architecture (Web Admin)

Folder roles (do not invent new top-level folders without asking):
- `app/(admin)/...` — route segments, one folder per module (roster,
  renewals, crm, plans, attendance)
- `components/ui/` — shadcn-style primitives only, no business logic
- `components/<module>/` — module-specific components, may import hooks
  but not call the API client directly (pass data down or use a hook)
- `lib/api/` — one typed function per API endpoint, all fetches live here
- `lib/hooks/` — React Query hooks that wrap `lib/api`
- `lib/auth/` — session + role + tenant helpers, server-only
- `lib/permissions/` — the permission-check functions (see
  security-data-access.mdc)

## Data flow
1. Server Component fetches initial data using `lib/api` (server-side call
   with the user's session token attached).
2. Client Components receive data as props, and use `lib/hooks` +
   React Query for mutations/refetches — never fetch directly in a
   `"use client"` component body.
3. Every API call in `lib/api` returns a typed result matching the
   Express API's response schema. If the schema is unknown, ask instead of
   inventing shape.

## Module boundaries
Match the PRD's M1–M13 modules. A component or route for M4 (Plans &
billing) should not directly import internals of M11 (CRM) — go through
`lib/api`. If a change looks like it needs to cross module boundaries,
say so before writing the code.
